Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect usage of the `filter->in_process` flag, which was intended to indicate whether a filter process was currently executing. The patch introduced a new flag `filter->in_process_callback` to properly track the state during the execution of the filter's process callback. The original logic incorrectly checked `filter->in_process` instead of `filter->in_process_callback`, leading to potential race conditions and incorrect scheduling behavior when the filter was being processed.
